.TH CTF-HUNTERCTL 1 "September 2026" "CTF Hunter 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctf-hunterctl \- inspect and control a local CTF Hunter daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctf-hunterctl --socket
.I PATH COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctf-hunterctl
sends one typed request to a running per-user daemon and prints its JSON
response. The socket option must be the first argument.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show daemon, collector, queue, notification, and capture health.
.TP
.B sessions
List sessions.
.TP
.BI create " NAME [PATTERN ...]"
Create a session.
.TP
.BI update " ID NAME [PATTERN ...]"
Update an inactive or paused session.
.TP
.BI start|pause|resume|stop " ID"
Change a session's lifecycle state.
.TP
.BI add-watch|remove-watch " ID DIRECTORY"
Add or remove a watched directory.
.TP
.BI watches " ID"
List watched directories.
.TP
.BI add-terminal|remove-terminal " ID TTY"
Add or remove a terminal source.
.TP
.BI terminals " ID"
List terminal sources.
.TP
.BI submit|preview " ID TEXT"
Persistently submit or non-persistently preview text analysis.
.TP
.BI list " ID [LIMIT]"
List findings for a session.
.TP
.BI finding " FINDING_ID"
Show one finding and its provenance.
.TP
.B shutdown
Request an orderly daemon shutdown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctf-hunter (1),
.BR ctf-hunterd (1)
